The design checker no longer slows down as it goes through a project when the
``too-many-*`` function messages are disabled but ``too-many-positional-arguments``
or ``keyword-arg-before-vararg`` is enabled: it kept a counter for every function
it had seen and updated all of them on each statement. The callbacks behind
``dict-iter-missing-items``, ``magic-value-comparison`` and
``unbalanced-dict-unpacking`` are now skipped when all the messages they check are
disabled.

Refs #11846
